; ARCHIVED - out of the manifest (tools/os88tithemus.py's SONGS) and so out
; of the MUSIC part. Put the name back in SONGS to hear it again. Why:
; its TONE became the Covenant's brief (chant, organ, bell); the song
; itself did not.
;
; TITHE - title theme, option 3: VESPERS
;
; The tithe as a SACRED debt. A plainchant line in D minor at 68 BPM - a row is
; an eighth of FOUR ticks, 219.7 ms - sung stepwise and never far from where it
; began, over an organ and a pedal, with a bell tolling on the drum channel.
; On the speaker it is one voice chanting, which is exactly what a chant is.
; A falls to the tonic through a C-sharp; B rises to D above and comes down.

song vespers "Vespers"
groove 4
unit 8
rows 16
measure 8
voice lead chant
voice bass pedal
voice chord organ

; --- the intonation: the voice alone, then the organ under it ------------------
lead VI1 = o4 d4 f4 g4 a4 | a2 g4 a4 |
lead VI2 = o4 >c4< a4 g4 f4 | g2. r4 |
bass BI1 = o2 r1 | d1 |
bass BI2 = o2 f1 | g1 |
chord CI1 = o3 r1 | [d f a]1 |
chord CI2 = o3 [c f a]1 | [d g b-]1 |
drum DI = b1 | b1 |

; --- A ------------------------------------------------------------------------
lead VA1 = o4 a2 g4 a4 | b-4 a4 g4 f4 |
lead VA2 = o4 g2 e4 c4 | d2 f4 e4 |
lead VA3 = o4 f4 g4 a4 >d4 | d4 c4< b-4 a4 |
lead VA4 = o4 g4 f4 e4 c+4 | d2. r4 |
bass BA1 = o2 d1 | <b-1> |
bass BA2 = o2 c1 | d1 |
bass BA3 = o2 f1 | <b-1> |
bass BA4 = o2 g2 a2 | d1 |
chord CA1 = o3 [d f a]1 | [d f b-]1 |
chord CA2 = o3 [c e g]1 | [d f a]1 |
chord CA3 = o3 [c f a]1 | [d f b-]1 |
chord CA4 = o3 [d g b-]2 [c+ e a]2 | [d f a]1 |
drum DA = b1 | r1 |
drum DA4 = b2 B2 | b1 |

; --- B: up to the D above -------------------------------------------------------
lead VB1 = o5 c4 d4 c4< a4 | b-2 a4 g4 |
lead VB2 = o4 g4 a4 b-4 >d4< | a2 e4 c+4 |
lead VB3 = o4 d4 f4 a4 >d4 | e2 d4 c4< |
lead VB4 = o4 b-4 >d4 c+4 e4 | d2. r4< |
bass BB1 = o2 f1 | <b-2> f2 |
bass BB2 = o2 g1 | a1 |
bass BB3 = o2 d1 | c1 |
bass BB4 = o2 <b-2 a2> | d1 |
chord CB1 = o3 [c f a]1 | [d f b-]2 [c f a]2 |
chord CB2 = o3 [d g b-]1 | [c+ e a]1 |
chord CB3 = o3 [d f a]1 | [c e g]1 |
chord CB4 = o3 [d f b-]2 [c+ e a]2 | [d f a]1 |
drum DB = B1 | r1 |

order VI1 BI1 CI1 DI
order VI2 BI2 CI2 DI
order VA1 BA1 CA1 DA          ; 2: the loop comes back here
order VA2 BA2 CA2 DA
order VA3 BA3 CA3 DA
order VA4 BA4 CA4 DA4
order VB1 BB1 CB1 DB
order VB2 BB2 CB2 DA
order VB3 BB3 CB3 DB
order VB4 BB4 CB4 DA4
loop 2
